:\"string\",\"description\":\"Applicable task/sample/settings/metric and direct relevance or transfer limits.\"},\"comparability\":{\"type\":\"string\",\"description\":\"Material differences or missing fields and resulting comparison limits; mark not applicable when appropriate.\"},\"confidence\":{\"type\":\"string\",\"description\":\"Qualitative strength plus evidence-based reason, separate from status/provenance; no fabricated probabilities.\"},\"disposition\":{\"enum\":[\"retain\",\"qualify\",\"reject\",\"unknown\"],\"description\":\"Evidence disposition, provisional until Main checks support and method.\"}}}},\"gaps\":{\"type\":\"array\",\"items\":{\"type\":\"string\"},\"description\":\"Named missing owned requirements, contradictions, access/budget limits and highest-impact resolving check.\"},\"stopReason\":{\"type\":\"string\",\"minLength\":1,\"description\":\"Actual sufficient-support, diminishing-return, access, budget or blocked-conclusion reason. Budget stops are not evidence saturation.\"}}}}","status":"completed","runner":"pi","kernel":"typescript","transport":"process","cwd":"/home/balauru/.pi-profiles/fabric/.worktrees/research-skill-rework","model":"openai-codex/gpt-5.6-terra","thinking":"high","startedAt":1788763245073,"updatedAt":1788763367048,"turns":6,"toolCalls":5,"text":"{\"assignment\":\"backups\",\"discovered\":[\"extensions.web_search\",\"extensions.fetch_content\",\"extensions.get_search_content\"],\"calls\":[{\"ref\":\"extensions.web_search\",\"args\":{\"queries\":[\"site:sqlite.org backup API online backup WAL locks official documentation\",\"site:postgresql.org docs current pg_basebackup online backup recovery official documentation\"],\"numResults\":5,\"includeContent\":false,\"workflow\":\"none\"},\"retrieved\":true,\"detail\":\"2/2 queries successful; 10 results total.\",\"responseId\":\"mtqvgvqc852i06\"},{\"ref\":\"extensions.fetch_content\",\"args\":{\"urls\":[\"https://www.sqlite.org/backup.html\",\"https://www.sqlite.org/c3ref/backup_finish.html\",\"https://www.sqlite.org/wal.html\",\"https://www.postgresql.org/docs/current/app-pgbasebackup.html\",\"https://www.postgresql.org/docs/current/continuous-archiving.html\",\"https://www.postgresql.org/docs/current/app-pgverifybackup.html\"],\"mode\":\"readable\"},\"retrieved\":true,\"detail\":\"6/6 official pages fetched; 143283 total characters.\",\"responseId\":\"mtqvh286k8nqsk\"},{\"ref\":\"extensions.get_search_content\",\"args\":{\"responseId\":\"mtqvh286k8nqsk\",\"urlIndex\":1,\"findText\":[\"source database is read-locked only while it is being read\",\"The destination database is written to in a transaction\",\"SQLITE_BUSY\",\"SQLITE_LOCKED\"],\"findMode\":\"case-insensitive\"},\"retrieved\":true,\"detail\":\"Retrieved SQLite page content; 1 matching passage, 3 requested text matches absent.\",\"responseId\":\"mtqvh286k8nqsk\"},{\"ref\":\"extensions.get_search_content\",\"args\":{\"responseId\":\"mtqvh286k8nqsk\",\"urlIndex\":3,\"findText\":[\"while the database server is running\",\"must have permission to execute the replication protocol\",\"will stream the write-ahead log\",\"A replication slot can be used to prevent the server from removing required WAL segments\"],\"findMode\":\"case-insensitive\"},\"retrieved\":true,\"detail\":\"Retrieved PostgreSQL pg_basebackup page content; 0 requested text matches.\",\"responseId\":\"mtqvh286k8nqsk\"}],\"rows\":[{\"id\":\"sqlite-online-backup\",\"slot\":\"backup\",\"finding\":\"SQLite's Online Backup API permits a live source database to be backed up while other connections read and write it; the destination remains in a write transaction for the backup duration.\",\"status\":\"documented_fact\",\"support\":[{\"url\":\"https://www.sqlite.org/c3ref/backup_finish.html\",\"title\":\"Online Backup API.\",\"passage\":\"SQLite holds a write transaction open on the destination database file for the duration of the backup operation. The source database is read-locked only while it is being read; it is not locked continuously for the entire backup operation. Thus, the backup may be performed on a live source database without preventing other database connections from reading or writing to the source database while the backup is underway.\",\"locator\":\"Online Backup API overview\",\"sourceType\":\"Primary documentation\",\"responseId\":\"mtqvh286k8nqsk\"}],\"method\":\"Documented API locking semantics, not a workload measurement. Applies to backups made through SQLite's Online Backup API.\",\"comparability\":\"This is a database-file/API backup mechanism, whereas PostgreSQL pg_basebackup is a physical cluster backup; no throughput comparison follows.\",\"confidence\":\"High for the stated API behavior because the decisive current primary documentation passage was retrieved.\",\"disposition\":\"retain\"},{\"id\":\"sqlite-wal-writer-limit\",\"slot\":\"operational-risk\",\"finding\":\"SQLite WAL mode still serializes writes: one WAL file permits only one writer at a time, so it does not make overlapping write transactions execute concurrently.\",\"status\":\"documented_fact\",\"support\":[{\"url\":\"https://www.sqlite.org/wal.html\",\"title\":\"Write-Ahead Logging\",\"passage\":\"However, since there is only one WAL file, there can only be one writer at a time.\",\"locator\":\"2.2 Concurrency\",\"sourceType\":\"Primary documentation\",\"responseId\":\"mtqvh286k8nqsk\"}],\"method\":\"Documented WAL locking model only; no workload, transaction duration, filesystem, or checkpoint configuration was measured.\",\"comparability\":\"Directly relevant to the defined overlapping-write requirement, but it does not quantify contention or latency.\",\"confidence\":\"High for the single-writer limitation because the official WAL page was retrieved; no performance conclusion is made.\",\"disposition\":\"retain\"},{\"id\":\"postgres-online-base-backup\",\"slot\":\"backup\",\"finding\":\"PostgreSQL documents pg_basebackup as taking a base backup from a running cluster without affecting other database clients, usable as a basis for point-in-time recovery or a standby.\",\"status\":\"documented_fact\",\"support\":[{\"url\":\"https://www.postgresql.org/docs/current/app-pgbasebackup.html\",\"title\":\"pg_basebackup\",\"passage\":\"pg_basebackup is used to take a base backup of a running PostgreSQL database cluster. These are taken without affecting other clients to the database, and can be used both for point-in-time recovery and as the starting point for a log-shipping or streaming-replication standby server.\",\"locator\":\"Description\",\"sourceType\":\"Primary documentation\",\"responseId\":\"mtqvh286k8nqsk\"}],\"method\":\"Documented physical-cluster backup behavior. It does not establish that a particular backup command, WAL-retention setting, or restore procedure is correct for a deployment.\",\"comparability\":\"Unlike SQLite's file-level API, this covers the PostgreSQL cluster. It supports only the online-backup semantic comparison, not measured operational cost.\",\"confidence\":\"Moderate: the current primary page was fetched, but the bounded exact-text search did not match the requested phrases, preventing additional extraction of WAL and recovery conditions.\",\"disposition\":\"qualify\"},{\"id\":\"postgres-wal-recovery-conditions\",\"slot\":\"operational-risk\",\"finding\":\"The retrieved PostgreSQL documentation supports that pg_basebackup is intended as a recovery base, but this child did not extract an exact current primary passage establishing the required WAL-capture, retention, and restore-verification conditions under writes.\",\"status\":\"unknown\",\"support\":[],\"counterevidence\":\"The current pg_basebackup, continuous-archiving, and pg_verifybackup pages were fetched, but the final bounded pg_basebackup content-match request returned zero matches for the requested WAL/privilege/retention phrases.\",\"method\":\"No deployment configuration or restore test was performed.\",\"comparability\":\"Not applicable until exact Postg